<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    What the system's widget PICKER shows (Android 12+, res/xml-v31's previewLayout). A copy of
    widget_unread.xml carrying an example COUNT and the label the widget usually wears. That is the
    only difference between the two files, and it is the right one: the runtime layout shows a
    horizontal ellipsis and the app's name, because until the provider's first draw the app knows
    neither the number nor which of the two labels applies, and must not pretend to. A picker entry
    reading "… / Sterna Mail" says nothing about what this widget is for, in the one place the
    widget has to sell itself before anyone places it.

    ⛔ Not drawn on the home screen, ever. The production layout is widget_unread.xml, and the
    number written HERE is an illustration that must never appear there: on a real cell it would sit
    as a plausible, wrong count for as long as the first draw takes, and forever if it never lands.

    The label is @string/inbox_all_inboxes — the widget's own two-account label, already translated
    in the nine languages, so the preview speaks the reader's language too. The figure is a literal:
    it is a digit, it would be the same word in every language, and a string for it would be a tenth
    translation to carry for a picture.
-->
<LinearLayout xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:layout_width="match_parent"
    android:layout_height="match_parent"
    android:background="@drawable/widget_unread_background"
    android:gravity="center"
    android:orientation="vertical"
    android:padding="8dp">

    <TextView
        android:id="@+id/widget_unread_count"
        android:layout_width="wrap_content"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:ellipsize="end"
        android:maxLines="1"
        android:text="12"
        android:textColor="@color/widget_unread_count"
        android:textSize="28sp"
        android:textStyle="bold" />

    <TextView
        android:id="@+id/widget_unread_label"
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:ellipsize="end"
        android:gravity="center_horizontal"
        android:maxLines="2"
        android:text="@string/inbox_all_inboxes"
        android:textColor="@color/widget_unread_label"
        android:textSize="12sp" />
</LinearLayout>
